[0.001, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\u001b[HPendingPermissionRegistry)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\nOriginal permission_request fired: true. After disconnectCurrent() + a reconnect attempt, the       \u001b[3;1HORIGINAL pending permission was still pending: true — proving the approval itself is\u001b[K\r\ndaemon-held/durable (PendingPermissionRegistry, keyed by requestId, independent of any HTTP         \u001b[5;1Hconnection). This exercises the fixture's own state, which mirrors permission-registry.ts:17-53 by  \u001b[6;1Hconstruction, not assistant-ui's runtime.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n[FAIL] 4b. reconnect-to-in-flight-turn capability\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\nA reconnect attempt that calls the real turn endpoint again (the only reconnect mechanism that      \u001b[10;1Hexists) got exactly one event back: [{\"kind\":\"chat_error\",\"message\":\"a chat turn is already in      \u001b[11;1Hprogress\"}]. There is no \"reattach to an in-flight stream\" API anywhere in\u001b[K\r\ndeus-native-chat-server.ts (confirmed by reading it end to end) — a reconnecting client can only    \u001b[13;1Hever be told a turn is already"]
[0.000, "o", " in progress, never rejoin it. This is graded FAIL, not PASS: the     \u001b[14;1Hcapability being tested (resuming an in-flight turn after reconnect) genuinely does not exist yet,  \u001b[15;1Hindependent of whether that failure was 'expected'.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n[FAIL] 5. approval resolution followed by resumed streaming\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\nrespondPermission() via the stateless requestId-keyed endpoint succeeded: true (the daemon-side     \u001b[19;1Happroval genuinely resolved). But the client-side runtime that originally asked for approval never  \u001b[20;1Hobserved ANY resumed output within 500ms (observed: false) — its connection generation had already  \u001b[21;1Hbeen superseded by the disconnect + reconnect-probe in scenario 4, so the daemon's later\u001b[K\r\nassistant_text/assistant_done emits had nobody left to write to (matches real res.writable\u001b[K\r\nsemantics: once a socket dies, later writes for that turn are silent no-ops, and there is no        \u001b[24;1HrequestId/turn-keyed buffer to replay). Confirmed NOT just delayed: after a full r"]
[0.000, "o", "estart, the reply \u001b[25;1His absent from persisted history too (persisted: false) — because history.append() for an assistant \u001b[26;1Hmessage only fires once its ChatModelAdapter generator RETURNS\u001b[K\r\n(local-thread-runtime-core.ts:568-577), and that generator is permanently stuck awaiting events that\u001b[28;1H will never arrive. Net: the daemon resumes internally and the approval is not lost, but the        \u001b[29;1Hresulting assistant output is unrecoverable through this transport shape as it exists today — the   \u001b[30;1Hspec's phrase \"approval resolution followed by resumed streaming\" does not hold for a genuinely     \u001b[31;1Hdisconnected+reconnected client.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n[PASS] 6. duplicate/out-of-order append protection (fixture-level: exercises Deus's \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\nstoreMessage/getMessagesSince semantics, not assistant-ui)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\nstoreMessage's real INSERT OR REPLACE-by-(id,chat_jid) semantics (db.ts:504-517) correctly collapsed\u001b[36;1H the retried duplicate into one row with the latest content, a"]
[0.000, "o", "nd getMessagesSince's real ORDER BY   \u001b[37;1Htimestamp (db.ts:555-587) correctly re-sorted the out-of-order pair chronologically regardless of   \u001b[38;1Hinsertion order. IMPORTANT CAVEAT: this protection comes entirely from Deus's OWN SQL schema/query  \u001b[39;1Hshape, not from assistant-ui — ThreadHistoryAdapter.append()'s contract\u001b[K\r\n(adapters/thread-history.ts:57-73) has no idempotency or ordering guarantee of its own; it is just  \u001b[41;1H\"a message was appended\". The library contributes nothing to this guarantee, it would only inherit  \u001b[42;1Hit by writing through Deus's existing store, unchanged.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[30m\u001b[42m\r\n[caprun] 0:sleep*\u001b[59X\u001b[45;77H\"unknow\" 06:46 28-Jul-26\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[44;1H\u001b[?2026l\u001b[18t\u001b[14t\u001b[?69h\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[?1006l\u001b[?1000l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1003l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[1;45r\u001b[1;45r\u001b[s\u001b[44;1H"]
